cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, protocol or data, please cite the archived release."
title: "rdnalink: a pre-registered test of linked SSU-ITS-LSU species calls, and a prototype package"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Brien"
    given-names: "Aaron"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ayobi/rdnalink"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23374303"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
abstract: >-
  Phase 0 protocol, amendments, code and fixed inputs for testing whether linking the SSU, ITS and LSU of one
  long rDNA read gives better species calls than the ITS alone, on the EUKARYOME v2.1 long-read set; and a
  prototype Python package (rdnalink) that runs the same method on any long reads. Protocols and outputs are
  CC BY 4.0 (DATA_LICENSE.md); EUKARYOME-derived reads keep EUKARYOME's CC BY 4.0 terms.
keywords:
  - rDNA
  - long reads
  - EUKARYOME
  - species identification
  - chimera detection
  - pre-registration
